00:10:23.255 --> 00:10:24.656
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.656 --> 00:10:26.892
All I know is that it'll be
awkward when they start the Zoom

00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:28.828
and Putin and Biden
are the first ones on.

00:10:28.828 --> 00:10:30.129
[ Laughter ]

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:33.165
"Stop video. Stop.
Hi, Joe. How's it going, man?"

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:34.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:36.936
During the summit,
Biden is expected to announce

00:10:36.936 --> 00:10:39.604
that the U.S. will cut
greenhouse gas emissions

00:10:39.604 --> 00:10:42.241
at least in half by 2030.

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:46.845
That's good. Yeah. Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:46.845 --> 00:10:49.448
Yeah, Biden plans to cut
emissions by 2030,

00:10:49.448 --> 00:10:50.482
at which point, it will be

00:10:50.482 --> 00:10:52.118
President Dwayne Johnson's
problem.

00:10:52.118 --> 00:10:54.920
[ Laughter ]

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.790
Hey, this is big. Remember that
European soccer Super League

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.458
that was just announced
two days ago?

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:01.393
-Yeah.
-Well, listen to this.

00:11:01.393 --> 00:11:04.229
-The proposed European
Super League may be over

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:06.432
before any teams
could even take the field.

00:11:06.432 --> 00:11:08.667 line:0%
The league announced it was
suspending current plans

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:11.136 line:0%
after the founding clubs
backed out of the venture,

00:11:11.136 --> 00:11:13.205 line:0%
just two days
after the initial announcement.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:16.642
-Wow. Only two days.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:16.642 --> 00:11:18.477
I've seen guacamole
last longer than that.

00:11:18.477 --> 00:11:19.979
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.979 --> 00:11:23.482
Seriously, the league crumbled
faster than a Nature Valley bar.

00:11:23.482 --> 00:11:25.083
-Oy, oh, hey!

00:11:25.083 --> 00:11:27.086
[ Rimshot ]
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.086 --> 00:11:29.020
-Yep, the Super League
has been knocked out

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:30.723
and, unlike most
soccer injuries,

00:11:30.723 --> 00:11:31.790
this one's real.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.358
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.358 --> 00:11:35.794
Now, those 12 teams are
showing up at their old leagues,

00:11:35.794 --> 00:11:37.863
trying to act like nothing
happened. It's like --

00:11:37.863 --> 00:11:38.964
[ English accent ]
Hey, what's up?

00:11:38.964 --> 00:11:40.666
Does anyone here watch
"Shite's Creek"?

00:11:40.666 --> 00:11:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:44.069
Dan Levy's fantastic.
He's brilliant. Yeah.

00:11:44.069 --> 00:11:45.704
You see the episode
where Moira is --

00:11:45.704 --> 00:11:46.872
Oh, sorry.
They're talking.

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:48.807
[ Laughter ]

00:11:48.807 --> 00:11:51.877
Some business news --
Netflix stock took a big dive

00:11:51.877 --> 00:11:53.045
this week after they reported

00:11:53.045 --> 00:11:55.814
a dramatic slowdown
in subscriber growth.

00:11:55.814 --> 00:11:57.783
-Ooh!
-It's a tough time for Netflix.

00:11:57.783 --> 00:12:00.119
Right now, executives are
fighting like two people

00:12:00.119 --> 00:12:01.954
looking for something
to watch on Netflix.

00:12:01.954 --> 00:12:03.321
[ Laughter ]

00:12:03.321 --> 00:12:05.557
Things are so bad,
the CEO of Netflix was like,

00:12:05.557 --> 00:12:08.194
"We either need a new
'Bridgerton' or a new pandemic."

00:12:08.194 --> 00:12:09.394
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.394 --> 00:12:11.797
But Netflix isn't letting
the news discourage them.

00:12:11.797 --> 00:12:15.500
They also announced that they're
spending more than $17 billion

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:17.302
on content this year.

00:12:17.302 --> 00:12:20.172
Yeah, they're spending
$17 billion for shows

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:22.208
that we're just going to listen
to while we're on Instagram.

00:12:22.208 --> 00:12:23.976
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.976 --> 00:12:27.313
Some more business news --
I saw that Lululemon is testing

00:12:27.313 --> 00:12:31.650 line:0%
a resale program where shoppers
sell and buy gently used items.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.385 line:0%
-Ooh. Ooh.

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:36.388
-Lululemon yoga pants.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:36.388 --> 00:12:38.190
Let me put this in perspective.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.727
Wearing a pair of lightly used
Lululemon pants is basically

00:12:41.727 --> 00:12:43.895
like picking up a pack
of lightly used Charmin.

00:12:43.895 --> 00:12:47.465
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:12:47.465 --> 00:12:50.635
I don't even know how you'd sell
used Lululemons.

00:12:50.635 --> 00:12:53.072
Anybody who wears them has
to cut them off with scissors.

00:12:53.072 --> 00:12:54.372
[ Laughter ]

00:12:54.372 --> 00:12:55.707
I don't know.
Maybe this'll work.

00:12:55.707 --> 00:12:57.376
I mean, how many times have you
seen someone walking out

00:12:57.376 --> 00:12:58.878
of a hot yoga class and thought,

00:12:58.878 --> 00:13:01.413
"I want those shorts,
that exact pair"?

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:02.981
[ Laughter ]

00:13:02.981 --> 00:13:04.350
Well, guys, you're not going to
believe this,

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.051
but the pandemic
has had an effect

00:13:06.051 --> 00:13:09.487
on the sales of Girl Scout
cookies. Listen to this.

00:13:09.487 --> 00:13:12.658 line:0%
-The lack of in-person sales
this year has left tons

00:13:12.658 --> 00:13:15.527 line:0%
of Thin Mints, Samoas,
and other flavors unsold.

00:13:15.527 --> 00:13:18.998 line:0%
-Troop leaders in Atlanta say
they have 700,000 boxes

00:13:18.998 --> 00:13:20.533 line:0%
just sitting in a warehouse.

00:13:20.533 --> 00:13:21.833
-Wow.

00:13:21.833 --> 00:13:23.369
I can't wait for my neighbor's
kid to be like,

00:13:23.369 --> 00:13:25.036
"Oh, hi, Mr. Fallon,
so I can put you down

00:13:25.036 --> 00:13:26.739
for 15,000 Do-Si-Dos?"

00:13:26.739 --> 00:13:28.007
[ Laughter ]

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:29.808
All I have to say is
you know America's broken

00:13:29.808 --> 00:13:31.676
when there's a surplus
of delicious cookies

00:13:31.676 --> 00:13:33.145
and life-saving vaccines.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:34.346
[ Laughter ]

00:13:34.346 --> 00:13:35.814
What are we doing?

00:13:35.814 --> 00:13:38.216
And get this -- in June,
New York City is getting

00:13:38.216 --> 00:13:42.621 line:0%
a 3-story, 21,000-square-foot
Harry Potter store.

00:13:42.621 --> 00:13:44.189 line:0%
-Ooh.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:13:44.189 --> 00:13:47.026
-It's exciting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:47.026 --> 00:13:48.960
I'd say there's
nothing hotter right now

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.363
than Harry Potter merchandise
and indoor shopping,

00:13:51.363 --> 00:13:52.431
would you agree?

00:13:52.431 --> 00:13:55.767
[ Laughter ]

00:13:55.767 --> 00:13:57.836
It'll be the first time
a New Yorker can whip out

00:13:57.836 --> 00:14:00.039
their wand on the subway
without getting pepper-sprayed.

00:14:00.039 --> 00:14:02.708
[ Laughter ]
What, what, what?!
-Hey, hey!

00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:04.843
Hey! Put away your Harry Potter.

00:14:04.843 --> 00:14:08.247
[ Laughter ]

00:14:08.247 --> 00:14:09.849
-I'm glad it's in New York City.

00:14:09.849 --> 00:14:11.182
I mean,
what's better than hearing,

00:14:11.182 --> 00:14:12.784
[ Brooklyn accent ]
"Welcome to the wizarding world

00:14:12.784 --> 00:14:13.852
of Harry Potter"?

00:14:13.852 --> 00:14:16.154
[ Laughter ]

00:14:16.154 --> 00:14:17.623
[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, the store is based on

00:14:17.623 --> 00:14:19.225
the previously
unreleased book...

00:14:21.393 --> 00:14:25.697
[ Laughter ]
"Honey, let's stop in here.
Do we need a wand?

00:14:25.697 --> 00:14:26.899
Oh, you answered
pretty quick there."

00:14:26.899 --> 00:14:28.500
[ Laughter ]

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.136
Well, there have been a lot
of incredible strides made

00:14:31.136 --> 00:14:33.672
in science over the past year,
but here's an invention

00:14:33.672 --> 00:14:35.674
you probably weren't expecting.
Watch this.

00:14:35.674 --> 00:14:37.977 line:0%
-Engineers at Purdue University

00:14:37.977 --> 00:14:41.012 line:0%
have created
the whitest paint ever.

00:14:41.012 --> 00:14:44.416 line:0%
They say the paint is so white
that coating a building with it

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.051 line:0%
could cool them off enough

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:49.254 line:0%
to reduce the need
for air conditioning.

00:14:49.254 --> 00:14:50.723
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:14:50.723 --> 00:14:52.557
Yeah, the "scientists" work

00:14:52.557 --> 00:14:55.327
at the distinguished
University of Benjamin Moore.

00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:56.461
[ Laughter ]

00:14:56.461 --> 00:14:58.230
Can we see
that paint color again?

00:14:58.230 --> 00:14:59.498
Yeah, looks like a photo

00:14:59.498 --> 00:15:01.467
from the Pillsbury Doughboy's
colonoscopy.

00:15:01.467 --> 00:15:03.101
[ Laughter ]
♪♪

00:15:03.101 --> 00:15:04.937
Today is Earth Day.

00:15:04.937 --> 00:15:06.972
Happy Earth Day!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:09.107
Everyone's in the spirit.
This morning at 7-Eleven,

00:15:09.107 --> 00:15:11.977
I saw a rat drinking a Big Gulp
with a metal straw.

00:15:11.977 --> 00:15:14.813
-Aww.
-Yes -- So, yes.

00:15:14.813 --> 00:15:16.582
A lot of stores
celebrated Earth Day.

00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:19.418
H&amp;M added a section
for sustainable items.

00:15:19.418 --> 00:15:21.720
Lowe's offered a free
Garden-to-Go kit,

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:24.089
and Subway recycled
last week's tuna.

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:26.124
-Oh.
-So, yeah, I thought that was --

00:15:26.124 --> 00:15:27.292
I'm kidding around,

00:15:27.292 --> 00:15:28.960
but protecting the Earth
is serious. I mean --

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.529
[ Valley accent ]
Can you believe that, in 1999,

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:32.665
we had nearly 50
Rainforest Cafes,

00:15:32.665 --> 00:15:34.433
and now we're down to almost 20?

00:15:34.433 --> 00:15:36.801
[ Laughter ]

00:15:36.801 --> 00:15:40.538
Think about it.

00:15:40.538 --> 00:15:42.274
That's right.
Today was all about the planet,

00:15:42.274 --> 00:15:43.408
and at the White House,

00:15:43.408 --> 00:15:45.544 line:0%
President Biden
hosted 40 world leaders

00:15:45.544 --> 00:15:48.046 line:0%
for a virtual
climate change summit.

00:15:48.046 --> 00:15:51.317
The tone of the summit
was that we're all responsible.

00:15:51.317 --> 00:15:53.285
But you know Costa Rica was
looking at the U.S. and China

00:15:53.285 --> 00:15:56.021
like, "Yeah.

00:15:56.021 --> 00:15:57.922
This is all our fault, right?
Yeah, we're --

00:15:57.922 --> 00:15:59.825
We're all to blame. Yeah.

00:15:59.825 --> 00:16:01.560
Huh. Yeah."

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.029
[ Laughter ]

00:16:04.029 --> 00:16:05.430
Now, of course,
with any virtual event,

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.000
you're going to have some
technical glitches, right?

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.801
But I didn't think
it'd be quite this bad.

00:16:09.801 --> 00:16:10.969
Take a look at what happened.

00:16:10.969 --> 00:16:13.238
-[ Echoing ] Good morning
to all our colleagues --

00:16:13.238 --> 00:16:14.707
all our colleagues
around the world,

00:16:14.707 --> 00:16:17.509
the world leaders taking part
in the summit, I thank you.

00:16:17.509 --> 00:16:19.311
-It's now my honor to call on

00:16:19.311 --> 00:16:21.713
His Excellency, the secretary
general of the United Nations,

00:16:21.713 --> 00:16:23.048
António Guterres.

00:16:23.048 --> 00:16:24.716
[ No audio ]

00:16:24.716 --> 00:16:25.850
[ Laughter ]

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:27.452
I now call upon
the Prime Minister

00:16:27.452 --> 00:16:29.854 line:0%
of the Republic of India,
His Excellency Narendra Modi.

00:16:29.854 --> 00:16:31.189 line:0%
-President Biden...

00:16:31.189 --> 00:16:32.858 line:0%
[ Phone dialing ]

00:16:32.858 --> 00:16:34.893 line:0%
...colleagues,

00:16:34.893 --> 00:16:36.428 line:0%
my fellow citizens.

00:16:36.428 --> 00:16:37.462 line:0%
[ Phone dialing ]

00:16:37.462 --> 00:16:38.930
-The floor is now to

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.299
the president
of the Russian Federation,

00:16:41.299 --> 00:16:43.969
Mr. Vladimir Putin.
Mr. President.

00:16:43.969 --> 00:16:46.705
[ Laughter ]

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:52.845
-What?

00:16:52.845 --> 00:16:53.945
[ Applause ]

00:16:53.945 --> 00:16:56.882
Looking.

00:16:56.882 --> 00:16:59.784
Somehow, we just flew
a helicopter on Mars,

00:16:59.784 --> 00:17:02.788
but we still can't get
a Zoom meeting to work.

00:17:02.788 --> 00:17:04.423
Next time, every leader
will be required

00:17:04.423 --> 00:17:06.592
to have at least
one grandchild present.

00:17:06.592 --> 00:17:07.826
[ Laughter ]

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:09.094
It's funny that we were
watching Putin

00:17:09.094 --> 00:17:10.529
and he didn't know
he was on-camera,

00:17:10.529 --> 00:17:12.698
'cause, usually,
it's the other way around.

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:14.032
[ Laughter ]

00:17:14.032 --> 00:17:15.066
Yeah.

00:17:15.066 --> 00:17:16.068
Even --

00:17:16.068 --> 00:17:17.068
-That was a good one.
-Preach?

00:17:17.068 --> 00:17:18.703
-That was good.

00:17:18.703 --> 00:17:21.406
-At one point, Britain's prime
minister, Boris Johnson, spoke

00:17:21.406 --> 00:17:24.642
and he used a pretty interesting
phrase to get his point across.

00:17:24.642 --> 00:17:25.677
Listen to this.

00:17:25.677 --> 00:17:28.914
-This is not all
about some expensive,

00:17:28.914 --> 00:17:31.650
politically correct green act

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.520
of -- of -- of bunny-hugging,

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.523
or however you want to put it.

00:17:37.523 --> 00:17:38.756
There's nothing wrong
with bunny-hugging,

00:17:38.756 --> 00:17:41.259
but you -- you know
what I'm driving at.

00:17:41.259 --> 00:17:43.294
-No.

00:17:43.294 --> 00:17:45.163
We have no idea
what you're driving at.

00:17:45.163 --> 00:17:46.231
[ Laughter ]

00:17:46.231 --> 00:17:47.499
At first, people were like, "Oh,

00:17:47.499 --> 00:17:50.468
is bunny-hugging a British
version of tree-hugging?"

00:17:50.468 --> 00:17:52.437
British people were like,
"No, he's just weird.

00:17:52.437 --> 00:17:54.973
I've never heard that term."

00:17:54.973 --> 00:17:56.575
That's right, leaders
from all over the world

00:17:56.575 --> 00:17:58.576
met to discuss
climate change over Zoom,

00:17:58.576 --> 00:18:01.780
and some even released joint
statements with President Biden.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:02.981
Check these out.

00:18:02.981 --> 00:18:04.950
After French President
Emanuel Macron said...

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.621
...Biden jumped in and said...

00:18:23.869 --> 00:18:25.570
[ Applause ]

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:27.405
I --
-Wow.

00:18:27.405 --> 00:18:28.806
-I don't really see
how that's relevant,

00:18:28.806 --> 00:18:31.075
but let's check out
another joint statement.

00:18:31.075 --> 00:18:33.145
After German Chancellor
Angela Merkel said...

00:18:37.149 --> 00:18:38.250
...Biden said...

00:18:51.296 --> 00:18:53.098
-Wait, what?!

00:18:53.098 --> 00:18:55.601
-What?!

00:18:55.601 --> 00:18:57.235
Like, why do they keep
letting him talk?

00:18:57.235 --> 00:18:58.503
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:18:58.503 --> 00:19:00.505
Let's check out one more.
-Alright, let's see it.

00:19:00.505 --> 00:19:02.374
-After British Prime Minister
Boris Johnson said...

00:19:06.144 --> 00:19:07.246
...Biden said...

00:19:24.228 --> 00:19:25.264
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:19:25.264 --> 00:19:27.499
-Wow.
-Ralph and Ralph?

00:19:27.499 --> 00:19:28.667
I don't know.

00:19:28.667 --> 00:19:29.701
-They sound like
"joint" statements.

00:19:29.701 --> 00:19:31.136
-I don't know, man.

00:19:31.136 --> 00:19:34.105
More news from Washington.
After the White House presented

00:19:34.105 --> 00:19:36.975
its $2.3 trillion
infrastructure plan,

00:19:36.975 --> 00:19:39.477
Republicans have responded
with their own version,

00:19:39.477 --> 00:19:42.581
that's only worth $568 billion.

00:19:42.581 --> 00:19:45.117
Yeah, Republicans want all these
repairs done on the cheap,

00:19:45.117 --> 00:19:48.120
which is why they're calling
the bill Operation Flex Seal.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.821
[ Laughter ]

00:19:49.821 --> 00:19:51.823
Biden has so much
on his plate -- infrastructure,

00:19:51.823 --> 00:19:54.525
construction, police reform,
military spending --

00:19:54.525 --> 00:19:56.928
right now, his to-do list
looks like the Village People.

00:19:56.928 --> 00:20:02.033
[ Laughter ]

00:20:02.033 --> 00:20:03.135
This is pretty incredible.

00:20:03.135 --> 00:20:04.536
I saw that Amazon is testing out

00:20:04.536 --> 00:20:06.404
a new way to pay at Whole Foods.

00:20:06.404 --> 00:20:07.672 line:0%
Take a look at this.

00:20:07.672 --> 00:20:10.509 line:0%
-Paying for groceries
with a swipe of your hand.

00:20:10.509 --> 00:20:13.044 line:0%
That could be coming soon
to Whole Foods stores near you.

00:20:13.044 --> 00:20:14.879 line:0%
It allows shoppers
to pay for items

00:20:14.879 --> 00:20:18.216 line:0%
by placing their palm
over the scanning device.

00:20:18.216 --> 00:20:20.118
-Here's how it works. You hover
your hand over the reader,

00:20:20.118 --> 00:20:21.986
then the cashier tells you
to stay still,

00:20:21.986 --> 00:20:25.090
then move it slightly,
then move it slightly again,

00:20:25.090 --> 00:20:27.058
and then you get frustrated
and pay with your credit card.

00:20:27.058 --> 00:20:28.827
-Wow. Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:20:28.827 --> 00:20:29.961
-Whatever. I think it's fun.

00:20:29.961 --> 00:20:33.065
I always wanted to buy plums
like I'm a Jedi.

00:20:33.065 --> 00:20:34.533
-Beep!

00:20:34.533 --> 00:20:37.002
[ Laughter ]

00:20:37.002 --> 00:20:38.136
-That's pretty good, right?

00:20:38.136 --> 00:20:40.005
-Beep. Yeah, that's
a pretty good Jedi.

00:20:40.005 --> 00:20:41.439
-Like, it's
the move back that's --

00:20:41.439 --> 00:20:43.008
-The move back
is what sells it. Yeah.

00:20:43.008 --> 00:20:44.542
That's just a guy.

00:20:44.542 --> 00:20:45.944
-Yeah.
-That's a Jedi.

00:20:45.944 --> 00:20:47.145
-Thank you.

00:20:47.145 --> 00:20:48.213
-Especially with the flourish.

00:20:48.213 --> 00:20:50.782
-Are they making another
"Star Wars" film?

00:20:50.782 --> 00:20:53.318
-I bet they -- Oh. You could --

00:20:53.318 --> 00:20:56.487
-I added a little mustard
on that last one.

00:20:56.487 --> 00:20:57.522
You want me to do it
one more time?

00:20:57.522 --> 00:20:58.624
-Do it one more time.
-Mr. Lucas?

00:20:58.624 --> 00:20:59.958
Okay.

00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:01.559
Step to the left? Yeah. More?

00:21:01.559 --> 00:21:02.594
-More?
-More?

00:21:02.594 --> 00:21:03.728
-How far?
-Okay, perfect.

00:21:03.728 --> 00:21:04.763
This is good?
-Do I have a car?

00:21:04.763 --> 00:21:06.397
-Okay.

00:21:06.397 --> 00:21:07.431
Thank you.

00:21:07.431 --> 00:21:11.269
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:21:11.269 --> 00:21:13.505
An Academy Award?

00:21:13.505 --> 00:21:16.008
Oh, it's not --
My name's not on it.

00:21:16.008 --> 00:21:17.408
-Oh, this isn't good.
McCormick said

00:21:17.408 --> 00:21:19.378
that they've had a difficult
time keeping up with demand

00:21:19.378 --> 00:21:22.213
for Old Bay Seasoning
during the pandemic.

00:21:22.213 --> 00:21:24.516
Can't really imagine why,
which brings us to a new segment

00:21:24.516 --> 00:21:26.584
we like to call
"Tariq's Teachable Moment."

00:21:26.584 --> 00:21:29.721
♪♪

00:21:29.721 --> 00:21:31.889
[ Applause ]

00:21:31.889 --> 00:21:34.726
-Thanks, Jimmy. I think
I can shine a light on this.

00:21:34.726 --> 00:21:37.629
You see, when Black people cook,

00:21:37.629 --> 00:21:39.931
we enjoy this thing
that you might have heard of.

00:21:39.931 --> 00:21:41.900
It's called flavor.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:42.934
[ Laughter ]

00:21:42.934 --> 00:21:45.236
Flavor is what happens to a meal

00:21:45.236 --> 00:21:48.540
when you add more to it
than just salt or pepper.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:50.575
-I don't know.
That sounds spicy.

00:21:50.575 --> 00:21:51.876
-It can be.

00:21:51.876 --> 00:21:55.947
In Black homes, spice racks
are like guard dogs --

00:21:55.947 --> 00:21:59.251
robust, loud, integral parts
of the family unit.

00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:03.255
Meanwhile, your spice rack
is more like a lap dog --

00:22:03.255 --> 00:22:07.458
small, decorative,
but ultimately useless.

00:22:07.458 --> 00:22:11.062
So, when the pandemic hit
and restaurants closed,

00:22:11.062 --> 00:22:14.232
Black people treated Old Bay
like it was toilet paper

00:22:14.232 --> 00:22:16.968
and bought enough
to fill a bunker.

00:22:16.968 --> 00:22:19.971 line:0%
-Okay, well, how much seasoning
should I use?

00:22:19.971 --> 00:22:21.439 line:0%
-A great start would be

00:22:21.439 --> 00:22:22.874 line:0%
more than zero.

00:22:22.874 --> 00:22:24.309 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:22:24.309 --> 00:22:26.111 line:0%
Just do what I do.

00:22:26.111 --> 00:22:28.513
Ignore the recipe
and sprinkle it on

00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:31.516
a little longer
than you usually would.

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:32.951
Like this.

00:22:32.951 --> 00:22:38.223
[ Laughter ]

00:22:38.223 --> 00:22:43.661
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:22:43.661 --> 00:22:45.563
-Okay, this seems like a lot.

00:22:45.563 --> 00:22:47.532
-It is.
That's the point, Jimmy.

00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:50.535
And, look, if you don't
understand, yet, that's okay.

00:22:50.535 --> 00:22:53.138
Just give it a minute
to marinate.

00:22:53.138 --> 00:22:54.439
[ Ding! ]

00:22:54.439 --> 00:22:59.177
[ Applause ]
♪♪

00:22:59.177 --> 00:23:00.712
-Tariq Trotter, everybody.
Tariq Trotter.

00:23:00.712 --> 00:23:02.047
I learned a lot.
Thank you, Tariq.

00:23:02.047 --> 00:23:05.417
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:23:05.417 --> 00:23:06.852
And, finally,
a woman in North Carolina

00:23:06.852 --> 00:23:08.720
was shopping at Target
when she found

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:11.256 line:0%
a surprise on the shelf.
Watch this.

00:23:11.256 --> 00:23:12.857 line:0%
-Aah!

00:23:12.857 --> 00:23:14.826 line:0%
-This is not something
you typically find

00:23:14.826 --> 00:23:17.729 line:0%
on the shelves in Target --
a black rat snake

00:23:17.729 --> 00:23:21.299 line:0%
slithering through the cans
of Bush's Baked Beans.

00:23:21.299 --> 00:23:22.967
-Ooh.
-Manager came on the PA system

00:23:22.967 --> 00:23:26.037
and was like, "Oh, hell, no,
in Aisle 5. Oh, hell, no."

00:23:26.037 --> 00:23:27.172
[ Applause ]
♪♪

00:23:27.172 --> 00:23:28.173
Well, we've all gotten used

00:23:28.173 --> 00:23:29.674
to wearing masks wherever we go,

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:33.345 line:0%
but I just read that the CDC
is looking into whether

00:23:33.345 --> 00:23:35.880 line:0%
it's still necessary
to wear them outdoors.

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:37.615 line:0%
-Oh?
-Ohh.

00:23:37.615 --> 00:23:39.418
-That's all this country
needs right now --

00:23:39.418 --> 00:23:41.386
Trevor,
the bartender from Señor Frog's,

00:23:41.386 --> 00:23:42.754
to have been right all along.
[ Laughter ]

00:23:42.754 --> 00:23:44.556
He's like, "I told you, bro!"

00:23:44.556 --> 00:23:47.125
[ Laughter ]

00:23:47.125 --> 00:23:48.959
I guess this is good,
although I was kind of

00:23:48.959 --> 00:23:50.028
looking forward
to another summer

00:23:50.028 --> 00:23:51.796
with bikini lines on my face,
you know?

00:23:51.796 --> 00:23:53.698
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:23:53.698 --> 00:23:54.966
-Honestly,
it would be nice to get back

00:23:54.966 --> 00:23:56.701
to when a masked man
outside your house

00:23:56.701 --> 00:23:58.336
was just a serial killer,
you know?

00:23:58.336 --> 00:24:00.371
[ Laughter ]

00:24:00.371 --> 00:24:02.306
Well, guys, it's a big weekend
for Hollywood.

00:24:02.306 --> 00:24:05.510
The 93rd annual Oscars
are this Sunday.

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:07.012
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:24:07.012 --> 00:24:09.013
Yeah.

00:24:09.013 --> 00:24:12.317
Of course, in quarantine, even
the Oscar statue gained weight.

00:24:12.317 --> 00:24:15.653
[ Laughter ]

00:24:15.653 --> 00:24:17.922
Yeah, it's gonna be a very
unique year for the Oscars.

00:24:17.922 --> 00:24:21.359
There's no host, no after party,
and no movies anyone saw.

00:24:21.359 --> 00:24:23.595
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:24:23.595 --> 00:24:25.397
-Yep, this year's Oscars
are about celebrating

00:24:25.397 --> 00:24:27.398
all the movies
we scrolled through and thought,

00:24:27.398 --> 00:24:29.401
"20 bucks? Nope."

00:24:29.401 --> 00:24:30.969
[ Laughter ]

00:24:30.969 --> 00:24:32.670
But this is interesting --
the Academy announced

00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:35.706
that masks are not required
while cameras are rolling,

00:24:35.706 --> 00:24:38.709
but should be worn
during commercial breaks.

00:24:38.709 --> 00:24:39.844
-Huh?
-Huh?

00:24:39.844 --> 00:24:41.679
-That makes sense.
-Yeah.

00:24:41.679 --> 00:24:43.348
-If we've learned anything
about the virus,

00:24:43.348 --> 00:24:45.283
it only spreads
during commercials.

00:24:45.283 --> 00:24:47.085
[ Laughter ]

00:24:47.085 --> 00:24:49.721 line:0%
And, speaking of movies, today,
"Mortal Kombat" was released

00:24:49.721 --> 00:24:52.590 line:0%
in theaters and on HBO Max.

00:24:52.590 --> 00:24:53.958
I haven't seen
the new "Mortal Kombat," yet,

00:24:53.958 --> 00:24:55.894
but I think I speak
for everyone when I say

00:24:55.894 --> 00:24:57.729
I just hope
it lives up to the play.

00:24:57.729 --> 00:25:00.165
[ Laughter ]

00:25:00.165 --> 00:25:03.034
Hey, check this out -- Netflix
is reportedly nearing a deal

00:25:03.034 --> 00:25:06.071
on an upcoming biopic
about the band KISS,

00:25:06.071 --> 00:25:07.772
called "Shout It Out Loud."

00:25:07.772 --> 00:25:09.574
Yeah, it's pretty exciting news.

00:25:09.574 --> 00:25:11.209
-[ Chuckling ]
Yeah, Jimmy, so exciting.

00:25:11.209 --> 00:25:12.777
[ Light laughter ]

00:25:12.777 --> 00:25:16.915
-Higgins, I didn't realize
you were such a big KISS fan.

00:25:16.915 --> 00:25:19.483
-What? No, no, no.
I just love biopics.

00:25:19.483 --> 00:25:22.320
[ Light laughter ]
-I-I see.

00:25:22.320 --> 00:25:23.754
Did you know in advance
that I'd be talking

00:25:23.754 --> 00:25:25.990
about a KISS biopic today?

00:25:25.990 --> 00:25:27.491
-No. Just took a chance.

00:25:27.491 --> 00:25:30.862
I wear KISS makeup to work
about half the time.

00:25:30.862 --> 00:25:32.197
-Alright.

00:25:32.197 --> 00:25:34.699
You can't wear that
during the show.

00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:36.234
-Ugh.

00:25:36.234 --> 00:25:38.069
Fine.

00:25:38.069 --> 00:25:40.271
You never support me, anyway.

00:25:40.271 --> 00:25:41.706
-Oh, come on.
I -- Thanks, buddy.

00:25:41.706 --> 00:25:44.208
I-I appreciate it.
-Oh, you know what?

00:25:44.208 --> 00:25:47.845
It's me. I'm sorry...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:25:47.845 --> 00:25:49.680
-Yeah.
Get this --

00:25:49.680 --> 00:25:52.617
starting on May 1st,
topless clubs in Las Vegas

00:25:52.617 --> 00:25:54.552
are officially allowed
to reopen.

00:25:54.552 --> 00:25:55.787
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:25:55.787 --> 00:25:57.155
Phew!

00:25:57.155 --> 00:25:58.923
Just in time for Mother's Day,
you know?

00:25:58.923 --> 00:26:00.425
[ Laughter ]

00:26:00.425 --> 00:26:02.593
If you're excited
about topless clubs reopening,

00:26:02.593 --> 00:26:04.596
I'm assuming
it was a long quarantine.

00:26:04.596 --> 00:26:05.863
[ Laughter ]

00:26:05.863 --> 00:26:07.999
Listen to this --
Nathan's is offering

00:26:07.999 --> 00:26:11.036 line:0%
5-cent hot dogs at Coney Island
this summer

00:26:11.036 --> 00:26:13.004 line:0%
for the first time in 100 years.

00:26:13.004 --> 00:26:16.207
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:26:16.207 --> 00:26:18.209
[ Applause ]

00:26:18.209 --> 00:26:19.944
Customers were like,
"Uh, I'd actually feel better

00:26:19.944 --> 00:26:21.346
if you charged more."

00:26:21.346 --> 00:26:22.614
[ Laughter ]

00:26:22.614 --> 00:26:24.349
5-cent hot dogs?

00:26:24.349 --> 00:26:26.618
I'd rather get
5-cent LASIK eye surgery.

00:26:26.618 --> 00:26:27.652
[ Laughter ]

00:26:27.652 --> 00:26:28.686
What?

00:26:28.686 --> 00:26:30.588
Eating a 5-cent hot dog
is as safe

00:26:30.588 --> 00:26:33.191
as taking home a mattress
on the street that says, "Free."

00:26:33.191 --> 00:26:36.627
[ Laughter ]

00:26:36.627 --> 00:26:38.162
"Seems like a good deal.
-"Hey. Yeah."

00:26:38.162 --> 00:26:39.364
-Let's take it
back to the house."

00:26:39.364 --> 00:26:40.565
[ Laughter ]

00:26:40.565 --> 00:26:42.466
Oh, I saw that Martha Stewart
just announced

00:26:42.466 --> 00:26:44.302 line:0%
the release
of her 99th cookbook.

00:26:44.302 --> 00:26:45.703 line:0%
-Whoo!
-Oh.

00:26:45.703 --> 00:26:48.573
-99. At this point,
the recipes are just...

00:26:51.442 --> 00:26:53.511 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-Wow. Rude.

00:26:53.511 --> 00:26:55.546
-It says, "Leave me alone,"
in the book.

00:26:55.546 --> 00:26:57.648
-Wow.
Very rude for a cookbook.

00:26:57.648 --> 00:27:00.551
-She would never.
Did you guys hear about this?

00:27:00.551 --> 00:27:03.488
An explosion
at a gender-reveal party --

00:27:03.488 --> 00:27:05.055
oh, my gosh --
in New Hampshire

00:27:05.055 --> 00:27:08.193
was so powerful that it damaged
[Chuckling] nearby homes

00:27:08.193 --> 00:27:10.962
and was felt in other states.
-What?

00:27:10.962 --> 00:27:13.131
-What? Like what's up with these
gender-reveal parties?

00:27:13.131 --> 00:27:15.266
Like --
-[ Laughs ]

00:27:15.266 --> 00:27:17.602
After the explosion, everyone
was like, "It's a...

00:27:17.602 --> 00:27:18.770
lawsuit!"

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:21.205
[ Laughter ]

00:27:21.205 --> 00:27:22.607
What is going on
with these things?

00:27:22.607 --> 00:27:23.808
-It's crazy.
-Yeah. They're supposed

00:27:23.808 --> 00:27:25.142
to reveal the gender
of the baby,

00:27:25.142 --> 00:27:26.977
not the IQ of the parent.

00:27:26.977 --> 00:27:29.881
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:27:29.881 --> 00:27:31.616
-Well, this made me laugh --
a man in Taiwan

00:27:31.616 --> 00:27:33.752
is making news for finding
an interesting way

00:27:33.752 --> 00:27:35.686
to get some extra time
off from work.

00:27:35.686 --> 00:27:36.788
Listen to this story.

00:27:36.788 --> 00:27:39.557
-A man in Taiwan
found a creative way

00:27:39.557 --> 00:27:42.460
to get an extended
vacation from work.

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:44.428
He initially got married
last April.

00:27:44.428 --> 00:27:46.597
He was given
eight days off.

00:27:46.597 --> 00:27:49.800
At the end of his leave,
he divorced his wife

00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:52.270
and planned to remarry her
the next day.

00:27:52.270 --> 00:27:55.640
And he did this whole process
not once, not twice,

00:27:55.640 --> 00:27:57.008
but three times.

00:27:57.008 --> 00:27:58.809
-[ Laughing ] Wow.

00:27:58.809 --> 00:28:00.144
Wow! Yeah.

00:28:00.144 --> 00:28:01.446
His boss knew something was up

00:28:01.446 --> 00:28:02.814
when he got a letter
that said...

00:28:05.250 --> 00:28:07.084
[ Laughter ]

00:28:07.084 --> 00:28:08.753
And, finally,
a woman here in New York City

00:28:08.753 --> 00:28:10.221
came home to her apartment

00:28:10.221 --> 00:28:12.256
and found an unexpected visitor.
Watch this.

00:28:12.256 --> 00:28:21.799
♪♪

00:28:21.799 --> 00:28:23.801
[ Audience groans ]
-What?!

00:28:23.801 --> 00:28:26.704
-Wow. I didn't even know
New York City pigeons laid eggs.

00:28:26.704 --> 00:28:28.139
[ Laughter ]

00:28:28.139 --> 00:28:30.175
I thought they were just rats
that earned their wings.

00:28:30.175 --> 00:28:35.112
[ Laughter ]

00:28:35.112 --> 00:28:37.548
Don't worry, though --
the pigeon's gone, and --

00:28:37.548 --> 00:28:40.485
this is no relation at all --
I just want to remind everyone

00:28:40.485 --> 00:28:44.255
about Nathan's 5-cent hot dogs
this summer on Coney Island.

00:28:44.255 --> 00:28:45.557
[ Cheers and applause ]
Happy summer, everybody!

